{
  "about": [
    "Shared test vectors for the per-decision outcome labels: the exporter's SQL (export_cohort_evidence.sh, section 2b) and label_decision in analyze_cohort.py must both give these answers. A future on-Mac resolver should be held to them too.",
    "Every time is seconds after the case's `base` (epoch seconds). An observation is [occurred_at, ended_at, category, classification_status, classification_confidence] and covers [occurred_at, ended_at); ended_at null is a row still open. Rows are listed in ledger (id) order.",
    "`expect` null means the exporter writes no row for that decision (it has no anchor). Otherwise every label is given; null is an empty cell.",
    "Bases in 2023 are in the past for any export run today; the base in 2099 keeps an open block's horizon in the future.",
    "A block may give `total_paused_seconds`, `paused_at` and `recovered_after_restart` (0 or 1, default 0). They decide only `observer_gap_cause`, which is empty unless `censor_reason` is observer_gap."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "returns_and_stays",
      "why": "The plain success: back at the anchor 30 s after the decision and there for the rest of the horizon. A medium-confidence row is evidence. A decision made at the anchor has no departure category and a return at 0 s. A decision with no anchor gets no row.",
      "base": 1700000000,
      "block": {"phase": "completed", "started_at": 0, "ended_at": 3000},
      "observations": [
        [0, 1000, "FOCUS_WORK", "classified", "high"],
        [1000, 1030, "SOCIAL_FEED", "classified", "high"],
        [1030, 2500, "FOCUS_WORK", "classified", "medium"],
        [2500, 3000, "COMMUNICATION", "classified", "high"]
      ],
      "decisions": [
        {"id": "v-warmup", "at": 100, "anchor": null, "verdict": "abstained_warmup", "expect": null},
        {"id": "v-returns", "at": 1000, "anchor": "FOCUS_WORK", "verdict": "offered",
         "expect": {"censor_reason": "none", "observer_gap_cause": null, "sustained_anchor_900s": 1, "departure_free_600s": 1, "seconds_to_sustained_return": 30, "departure_category": "SOCIAL_FEED"}},
        {"id": "v-at-anchor", "at": 1030, "anchor": "FOCUS_WORK", "verdict": "abstained_block_cap",
         "expect": {"censor_reason": "none", "observer_gap_cause": null, "sustained_anchor_900s": 1, "departure_free_600s": 1, "seconds_to_sustained_return": 0, "departure_category": null}}
      ]
    },
